<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasyl Chuchupak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasyl Chuchupak was a Ukrainian insurgent leader who in 1919 organised a peasant self-defence force around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/motronynskyi-monastery">Motronynskyi Monastery</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kholodny-yar">Kholodny Yar</a> forest of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Declaring loyalty to the Ukrainian People's Republic, the Kholodny Yar Republic controlled some twenty villages and fought both White and Red armies. He was killed in a clash with Soviet forces in 1920.</p></div>
